<!-- ============ THESIS (the answer, in words) ============ -->
<section class="thesis" id="thesis">
  <div class="wrap tgrid">
    <blockquote class="tquote rv">The bundle is the interface. Specifications, <button class="kchip-gloss" type="button" data-gloss="boq">BOQs</button>, <button class="kchip-gloss" type="button" data-gloss="atc">ATCs</button>, corrigenda, annexures. Each carries a clause that can win the bid <em class="it">or end it.</em> Reading is not the work. Reconstruction is.</blockquote>
    <aside class="tmargin rv" aria-label="Margin annotations">
      <div class="tnote"><span class="tn-k">Document intelligence</span><p>The bundle is parsed locally, page by page, into structured requirements.</p></div>
      <div class="tnote"><span class="tn-k">Compliance reconstruction</span><p>Eligibility, instruments and certifications are rebuilt as checkable claims.</p></div>
      <div class="tnote"><span class="tn-k">Decision traceability</span><p>Every verdict carries its clause and page: at rest, not on hover.</p></div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

