        <h3>KRISEVA TAS</h3>
        <p class="vsub">Bidder-side tender intelligence and bid review for defence <button class="kchip-gloss" type="button" data-gloss="msme">MSMEs</button> and defence-tech teams. A scattered bundle becomes a defensible <b>BID / REVIEW / SKIP</b> decision. Recommendation only; the operator signs. <button class="kchip-claim" type="button" data-claim="tas.one-liner" aria-label="Provenance: TAS one-liner">c2</button></p>
        <ul class="caps">
          <li><span>Treats tenders as <b>bundles</b>: bid documents, specifications, BOQs, ATCs, corrigenda, annexures.</span><span class="ref">bundle-aware</span></li>
          <li><span>Parses PDF, DOCX, XLSX, TXT and CSV tender files <b>locally</b>, with local OCR for scanned pages.</span><span class="ref">on-premise</span></li>
          <li><span>Extracts metadata such as buyer fields, dates, values, <button class="kchip-gloss" type="button" data-gloss="emd">EMD</button>/<button class="kchip-gloss" type="button" data-gloss="epbg">ePBG</button> and eligibility signals, <b>with provenance</b>.</span><span class="ref">clause + page</span></li>
          <li><span>Live <b><button class="kchip-gloss" type="button" data-gloss="gem">GeM</button></b> discovery and acquisition; <button class="kchip-gloss" type="button" data-gloss="defproc">DefProc</button> public discovery with operator-assisted flows for protected documents.</span><span class="ref">operator-gated</span></li>
          <li><span>Operator review briefs with <b>BID / REVIEW / SKIP</b> recommendations. No autonomous authority.</span><span class="ref">committee-assist</span></li>
        </ul>
