<!-- X7: guided walk caption chip -->
<div class="tourchip" id="tourChip" role="dialog" aria-label="Guided walk" aria-live="polite">
  <div class="tc-k"><span id="tourPos">ACT 00 · 1/10</span><span>→ next · ← back · esc exits</span></div>
  <p class="tc-s" id="tourLine"></p>
</div>

<!-- X1: claim-chip registry, baked from publicClaims.ts at build -->
<script type="application/json" id="claimRegistry" set:html={JSON.stringify(claimRegistry)}></script>
<script is:inline defer src="/js/kriseva-chips.js"></script>

<!-- BUILD NOTES ==================================================
CONCEPT - "Evidential Cartography: the dossier, alive."
The site is a living procurement dossier. The WebGL hero makes the thesis
literal: a tender bundle (ink-outlined planes) emits brass evidence strands
(CatmullRom tubes drawn on scroll via setDrawRange) to floating clause nodes;
as each strand completes, its clause label resolves into a six-state verdict
chip; at the end of the pinned scroll the nodes assemble into a slowly
rotating verdict ledger. Everything below is evidence-as-interaction:
matrix → audit chain → radar → boundary. No decoration.

SECTION MAP
nav · hero (pinned, scrubbed, 230% scroll) · dual opposing marquees ·
§01 two volumes (TAS w/ scrubbed 6-stage pipeline, Evaluator) · thesis pull-quote ·
§02 evaluation matrix (click cell → source clause + reasoning + HITL routing) ·
§03 audit chain (verify / tamper / reset, navy) · §04 bidability radar ·
§05 the Boundary (Zone I vs dashed explicit egress) · stats count-ups ·
§06 field record · contact · footer.

SAFETY / FALLBACKS
- no-JS: html.js never set → all reveal states stay visible; page fully legible.
- prefers-reduced-motion: no Lenis, no pin/scrub, no marquees, no count-ups,
  static SVG hero plate.
- mobile / coarse pointer / no WebGL: static SVG hero plate; all interactive
  modules are click/tap-driven buttons.
- WebGL: DPR ≤ 1.75, ~60fps cap, render loop skips when off-screen or
  document.hidden.

PORTING TO ASTRO (Kriseva_website_v1-main/website/)
